## [TAB CONTAINER — horizontal, 4 tabs]

### TAB 1: NMEA

**NMEA (Zero) account**

Required before anything else — this is the protected identity used for all downstream access.

- This is a protected system. You must have a NMEA (Zero) account and open the connection to the gateway via a PAS 2.0 RDP connection.
- Not sure if you already have one? Check `portal.azu`.
- If you don't have a NMEA account yet, it can be created during the ePAS request (see the ePAS tab, "Strong Authentication Token" section) using the naming convention `VBA\[WINDOWSNAME]0`.

> **[Panel macro — warning]**
> **If you already have an ePAS in flight:** Clone the in-progress one and submit based on that copy. Starting a fresh request instead of cloning can wipe existing access or lose what's currently in flight.

---

### TAB 2: ePAS

**Prerequisites for DB access**

You need CyberArk (PIV option) **plus** the ePAS group/role — both are required, not either/or.

- CyberArk – PIV access
- One of these ePAS groups/roles assigned to your NMEA account: `vaecwins-gateway-nprod`, `vaecwins_ateway-prod`, `CldWinS_Dev`

**Part A — Submit the ePAS request**

Portal: https://epas.r02.med.va.gov/apps/myva/

1. Go to the ePAS portal and select **Submit Request** — you'll be redirected to the Assignee tab.
2. **Assignee Information.** Name, email, and domain are usually pre-populated — fill manually if not.
   - Domain: `[VBA/WINDOWSNAME]`
   - Employee type: Contractor
   - Date of birth: MM/DD/YYYY
   - SSN: 000-00-0000 format
3. **Expiration of Elevated Privileges.** "Date Expires" = your PIV expiration date.
4. **Strong Authentication Token.** Only one NMEA is required.
   - If you have a NMEA account, enter it including the domain name.
   - If not, enter a name in the blank field to create one, using: `VBA\[WINDOWSNAME]0`
5. **Supervisor/COR.**
   - Name: Corona, Jose
   - Email: Jrona@vakk

**Part B — CyberArk + PAS (PIV option)**

1. Create a new EPAS document and request access for your zero account to one of the three groups listed above.
2. Choose **Submit New Request**.
3. Select your PIV card expiration date in the "Date Expires" field.
4. Under Supervisor/COR, select **Lookup**, enter `Corona, Jose`, hit enter, and select the name in the popup.
5. Switch to the **Roles** tab.
6. In the purple box, select a role under **Standard Role**, then click **Add Selected Role**.

   Justification field:
   `<enter NMEA account> - As a <enter role> I require access to the VA PAS System PIV/PIV Cert with PAS to access DB Gateway servers.`

7. In the pink box (**Groups that represent a Role**), set **Systems Reside In** → **Infrastructure Operations**. In the popup, search `VA PAS`, select **VA PAS Users**, click OK.

   Justification/Details field:
   `<NMEA account> - I require access to the VA PAS System PIV/PIV Cert with PAS solution to perform my work as a <enter your role>.`

**Part C — Add DB Gateway Servers (RDP) to the same request**

1. Still in the pink box, under **Groups that represent a role**, set **Systems Reside In** → **VA Enterprise Cloud**.
2. Select **Select Groups to Add**. In the popup, search `vaecwins_aws_lgy-rds-gateway`.
3. Select both groups: `vaecwins_aws_lgy-rds-gateway-nprod` and `vaecwins_aws_lgy-rds-gateway-prod`, then click OK. This adds two lines to the bottom of the document — select your 0 account on that line.

   Justification/Details field:
   `As a <enter your role>, I require RDP access to Non-Prod LGY Environments for my NMEA account to support QA testing/development efforts.`

4. Click **Submit & Submit** (top left) to send the document for approval and processing.

