### TAB 3: SNOW

**SNOW ticket**

Only submit this after your Jira and ePAS approvals are complete — it hands off to the Ops team for provisioning.

> **[Panel macro — red/warning]**
> **Format matters:** A ticket that doesn't follow the description format below is not correct and will be closed with no action.

**Service Request Description — copy, personalize, paste:**

```
Please add to my PIV account to vaecwins_aws_lgy-RDS-gateway-nprod on vac10raslgy811.va.gov

As a QA tester/developer/project lead, I need access to this server to support LGY sustainment efforts until end of contract.

If required, my NMEA account is OITWAS.

DSO-345 is approved.
```

1. Paste and personalize the description above (swap in your own server target, role, and NMEA account).
2. Click **Order Now**.

---

### TAB 4: Connect

**Connect via CyberArk**

Final step, once all four prior steps are approved and provisioned.

1. Confirm Jira ticket, ePAS request, and SNOW ticket are all approved/completed.
2. Log in via CyberArk and connect to the RDS instance through the RDP gateway.

